1:09:261 Stunde, 9 Minuten, 26 Sekundenusing just one. The other language is always there, humming in the background, exerting subtle influence. So, what does
1:09:361 Stunde, 9 Minuten, 36 Sekundenall this add up to? I think it points toward a picture of human cognition that's far more flexible and far more
1:09:441 Stunde, 9 Minuten, 44 Sekundenlanguage sensitive than the strong universalist position would suggest, but also far more resilient and creative than the strong position implied.
1:09:551 Stunde, 9 Minuten, 55 SekundenYou're not trapped by your language, but you're not independent of it either.
1:10:001 Stunde, 10 MinutenYou're in a dance with it. And if you learn new languages, you learn new dances.
1:10:071 Stunde, 10 Minuten, 7 SekundenNow, around the same time that bilingualism research was producing these insights, another group of
